This fork (https://github.com/ChristianHovenbitzer/graphify-al) adds support
for the AL programming language (Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central):

  - graphify/detect.py  — `.al` registered as a code extension
  - graphify/extract.py — _AL_CONFIG, extract_al, _al_collect_facts,
                          _resolve_al_facts (AL semantic layer)
  - graphify/serve.py   — _RoutedGraph, _find_node_by_global_id and the
                          country/version/global_id routing built on top of
                          it (bc-code-atlas multi-tenant serving)
  - AL_SUPPORT.md, examples/ — fork documentation and a sample

AL modifications Copyright (c) 2026 the fork authors. Contributed under the
MIT License prior to the relicensing above (see LICENSE-MIT); AL
modifications made from that point on follow the upstream project and are
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, consistent with the rest of
this package.

AL parsing uses tree-sitter-al (https://github.com/SShadowS/tree-sitter-al),
an independent MIT-licensed grammar, consumed as a normal Python dependency
(not redistributed in this repository).
